assertion  XSH.cacosh.015
anchor     functions/cacosh.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       cacosh of +Inf + iNaN, of -Inf + iNaN and of NaN + iInf is +Inf +
           iNaN.
note       The tag on this passage is the IEC 60559 Complex Floating-Point
           option; the test is NOTINUSE unless the C implementation claims it
           (Annex G of the C standard). No error is defined on this page, so
           errno is not examined; an exception is checked only when
           math_errhandling includes MATH_ERREXCEPT.
test       t/015-inf-nan.c

assertion  XSH.cacosh.016
anchor     functions/cacosh.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       cacosh of the conjugate of z returns the conjugate of cacosh of z,
           part for part (equal values, zero signs included, NaN matching
           NaN), at ordinary points, at real-axis points where branch cuts
           lie, and at points with infinite parts and with a NaN real part.
note       The tag on this passage is the IEC 60559 Complex Floating-Point
           option; the test is NOTINUSE unless the C implementation claims it
           (Annex G of the C standard). No error is defined on this page, so
           errno is not examined; an exception is checked only when
           math_errhandling includes MATH_ERREXCEPT. Points with a NaN
           imaginary part are left out (and, for the odd and even rules,
           points with any NaN part): the sign of a NaN carries no required
           meaning. See Q-113.
test       t/016-conjugate-symmetry.c
